name: "my-xymon-extensions"
version: "@VERSION@"
origin: "net-mgmt/my-xymon-extensions"
comment: "Portable Xymon client extensions (SMART disk monitoring)"
www: "https://github.com/roemer2201/my-xymon-extensions"
maintainer: "r.oliver@web.de"
prefix: "/usr/local"
categories: ["net-mgmt"]
desc: "Custom monitoring tests (extensions) for the Xymon systems monitor.

Included extensions:
* smart - S.M.A.R.T. disk health monitoring for SATA/ATA, NVMe and
  basic SAS disks, with vendor-normalized metrics, thresholds and
  per-disk RRD graphing support. (The eMMC health support of this
  extension is Linux-only and inactive on FreeBSD.)
* la - load average with per-CPU-core thresholds (task disabled by
  default: the Xymon client already covers this on full clients).
* disk - filesystem usage from df with global and per-mount
  thresholds, reporting into the standard "disk" column (task
  disabled by default: the Xymon client already covers this on full
  clients).
* temp and memory - Linux-only (hwmon sysfs, /proc/meminfo); they
  report a clear status on FreeBSD.
* fritzdsl - AVM FRITZ!Box DSL line monitoring via TR-064: line
  state, sync rate, noise margin, attenuation and error counters
  with thresholds and RRD graphing support. Polls the box from the
  Xymon server; requires ftp/curl and ships disabled until
  configured.
* fritzwan - AVM FRITZ!Box WAN throughput monitoring: physical link
  state, average throughput, link capacity and utilization from the
  box's 64-bit UPnP counters (TR-064 fallback). Polls the box from
  the Xymon server; requires ftp/curl and ships disabled until
  configured.
* wifi - Wi-Fi access point metadata. Linux-only (iw/nl80211);
  reports a clear status on FreeBSD and ships disabled.
* if_link - link state changes per network interface, counted from
  the kernel's carrier counters, with optional per-port thresholds.
  Linux-only (there is no equivalent counter on FreeBSD, and polling
  the current state would miss short flaps); reports a clear status
  on FreeBSD - comment its clientlaunch.d snippet out to hide the
  column.

Requires net-mgmt/xymon-client and sysutils/smartmontools (>= 7.0).
Activation steps (sudoers rule, clientlaunch.d include, server-side
graphs)
are documented in share/doc/my-xymon-extensions/."
